 #uuid "d0d2bfed-fc08-50a9-93f7-83f4384c1054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092902 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186091612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092902 #edb/ref 1069 "q-9341" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092902 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092902 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4ecc70e1-e461-5246-9098-c27aa6c114e3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092903 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186091618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092903 #edb/ref 1069 "q-9346" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092903 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092903 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d64c1c7-5e2c-5d9e-ad36-647b8fb50a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093069 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093069 #edb/ref 1061 20080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093069 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "aa3f5d68-5f04-578d-b46e-4900e8496c29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093069 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093070 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093070 #edb/ref 1061 20082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093070 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "89493310-e194-5bc4-bea0-893a5af03e16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093070 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093071 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093071 #edb/ref 1061 20083 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093071 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04fc546d-cc73-521c-b37b-04a57e324df2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093071 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093072 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093072 #edb/ref 1061 20084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093072 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75bc9629-a0a2-557a-b062-e66b006ea327" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093072 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093073 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186093071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093073 #edb/ref 1061 20085 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093073 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "78e02a6a-545a-511e-a2f5-b45e357cb0fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093073 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093074 #edb/ref 1061 20087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093074 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75d3f2ae-a3c8-5016-8ccf-895f6655ebd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093074 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093438 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the matrix ![](images/63/63dd03e425762fa8e9e2e0d33ce552245c6d1c00a12022c433329c3c747cdbba.svg) How can we find its eigenvalues?\n\nBy definition, we need to find the value(s) of $\\,\\lambda\\,$ such that $\\,A\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v} = \\lambda \\mathbf{\\color{blue}v}\\,$ is true for some *non-zero* vector $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v}.$ Let's re-write this equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =\\lambda v \\\\ Av-\\lambda v & =0 \\\\ Av-\\lambda Iv & =0 \\\\ (A-\\lambda I)v & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation above tells us that there should be at least one non-zero vector $\\mathbf{\\color{blue}v}$ that lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A-\\lambda I)$, the null space of the matrix $A-\\lambda I.$ As a result, the invertible matrix theorem tells us that the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\,$ must be singular, meaning $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0.$\n\nWe've reduced the problem to finding the values of $\\lambda$ that satisfy the equation\n\n$$\n\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0,\n$$\n\nwhich is called the **characteristic equation** of the matrix $A$. So, let's solve it!\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix $A-\\lambda I\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\,-\\,\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\,-\\,\\lambda [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\,-\\,\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ -1 & -4\\,-\\,\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the characteristic equation $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ -1 & -4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-5\\cdot (-1) & =0 \\\\ -8-2\\lambda +4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues of $A$ are $\\lambda=-3$ and $\\lambda=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093438 #edb/ref 1065 3559 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093438 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "992adb24-3547-5b71-bb96-561b2f90f721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093438 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093439 #edb/ref 1064 "The characteristic equation of any $2 \\!\\times\\! 2$ matrix $A$ is always a quadratic equation, which implies that $A$ has at most $2$ eigenvalues. Here are the all possible cases:\n\n- Two distinct real eigenvalues\n\n- One repeated real eigenvalue (or, equivalently, two real eigenvalues that are the same)\n\n- No real eigenvalues (or, equivalently, two complex eigenvalues)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093439 #edb/ref 1065 3560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093439 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3ec52280-5c5a-5e6f-bcbe-328634cbfecf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186093439 #edb/ref 1067 "The Number of Real Eigenvalues of a 2x2 Matrix" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241427 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241427 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241427 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1d5cd195-916d-51d3-a145-ac3d8abbdf92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241571 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +40=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241571 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241571 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2bdfc526-d86a-5e73-baca-2112c1ad2358" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241646 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -40=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241646 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241646 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "35403cd9-ea2a-5b57-971f-4e9e59069317" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242639 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242639 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186242639 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a5cf22be-62ee-5bda-9228-41b20aca0652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243148 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +10=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dd32357c-ec00-5793-bb30-3f656df8bc88" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186241427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186241571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186241646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186242639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186243148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186241427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186243729 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9d00855c-44e0-5a49-b0df-a66417f8be4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186243729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1069 "q-107987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11ba9d38-2921-5184-bf8a-8d9ae2f12bf8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186244111 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the characteristic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (8-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-6\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ -40-8\\lambda +5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2} & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -40 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1069 "q-36780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1fda33b2-0f78-5ef6-abce-da9e465c13f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402509 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(P-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -5 & 7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )-1\\cdot (-5) & =0 \\\\ 49-7\\lambda -7\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-14\\lambda +54 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the discriminant of the quadratic equation above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =(-14)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot 54 \\\\  & =196-216 \\\\  & =-20 \\\\  & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the characteristic equation does not have real solutions and therefore $P$ does not have real eigenvalues." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402511 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402510 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9c905a94-1e61-56fb-85f0-520ef6a3631a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402511 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\lambda =7$ (double root)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402511 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402511 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5ad3afc0-1147-5a90-b327-46c419abae45" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402512 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =7$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402512 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402512 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bebf86c2-9d02-56e0-8de7-e3c093fdb99b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402513 #edb/ref 1080 "There are no real eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402513 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402513 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1fe3b5b3-5b53-5af3-a386-d1a9cac7570e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402514 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\lambda =7$ and $\\lambda =-5$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402514 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402514 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e1b2964-fbf6-54e9-a3dc-5eb4004c5b91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402515 #edb/ref 1080 "$\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402515 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921