92186045417] [17592186426466 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426466 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6ff870f2-a00f-5d9f-a34a-712ea4371cad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1071 "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95fd78c2-6907-5df8-b9fe-1452968ce01b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426471 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(\\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429726 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186429726 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account linear: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: linear=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; 